SkyAt←{
   ⍝ Positions of stars, sun, moon, planets and comet for one observation
   ⍝ ⍵ is STATEDDAYNO STATEDTIME LAT LONG: Julian day number of the
   ⍝ stated date, stated time (UTC hours), latitude and longitude (degrees
   ⍝ north and east). The result holds the inputs and every calculated position.
    day stated lat long←⍵
    time←long TimeAdjust stated
    date←day+(time÷24)-long÷360
    sky←⎕NS ⍬
    sky.(StatedDayNo StatedTime Lat Long Time Date)←day stated lat long time date
    sky.(Planets PlanetsAA PlanetsVisible PlanetCoord Phase VisiblePlanetsAA)←CalculatePlanets lat,date,time
    sky.(StarsVisible BrightVisible BrightStarsAA StarCoord)←CalculateStars lat,date,time
    sky }
